{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790761395,"nonce":"PsLvHlLBxaitxTrP0qyVeoFth34=","message":"\u003c!-- ABOUTME: Records the verified experimental desktop sketch-gallery landing. --\u003e\n\u003c!-- ABOUTME: Distinguishes browser scope changes and automated evidence from outstanding native GUI acceptance. --\u003e\n\n## Experimental landing\n\nFabian explicitly authorized landing the desktop feature for experimentation and withdrew browser/PWA Description authoring for now. Description is now desktop-only: browser/PWA defaults and restored layouts omit the panel, and browser save/download/recovery remains source-only. Accepted recovery snapshots with missing or non-string display names no longer crash browser startup.\n\nVerified published commit: `4ef3d5d34c07ae30c343965498df6e8577c12a8f` on `origin/main`.\n\nhttps://github.com/ff6347/giclang/commit/4ef3d5d34c07ae30c343965498df6e8577c12a8f\n\nThe regular merge preserves main's intervening math, examples, beta versions, and macOS packaging changes. GPT-6 Luna performed implementation and candidate verification; GPT-6.1 Sol approved the merged code. The separately approved phyllotaxis formatting commit only adds a terminal newline; authored text and frontmatter values are unchanged.\n\n## Exact-candidate verification\n\nOn published SHA `4ef3d5d`: frozen installation and diff check; 427 core/CLI tests; 639 compact tests; package and browser typechecks; lint and formatting; browser build; 97 Firefox tests with 8 established tutor skips; 9 PWA lifecycle tests; 159 native tests with 1 intentionally ignored paid live-provider test; Rust formatting and Clippy; and desktop packaging all passed. Only the established Monaco large-chunk build advisory remained. Raw local logs: `/tmp/candidate-4ef3d5d/`.\n\nThe final documentation commit carries `[skip ci]`, so Pages was explicitly dispatched for the published SHA and verified successful:\n\nhttps://github.com/ff6347/giclang/actions/runs/36696646100\n\nFresh local experimental desktop outputs: `GiC.app` and `GiC_0.9.0-beta.1_aarch64.dmg` in the feature worktree's desktop bundle directory. DMG SHA-256: `3ba844cedfd8f9d3134ae639f3b98df31b14e4639e1553ad62a805270853b21f`.\n\n## Remaining acceptance\n\nThis is an experimental landing, not full release acceptance. The packaged app was built but its real macOS UI/native-dialog workflows have not been exercised: description Save/Save As/open/clear and failure/cancellation; gallery selection/discard, restart/project switching, inert Markdown; real Canvas-to-PNG equality/no rerun and broken-source thumbnail preservation; and immutable Examples still need native acceptance. Keep this feature issue open for that work and any concrete bugs found during experimentation. No parent PRD or broad context request has been changed or closed.","files":null}]}